      "notes": "Anusvara is a homorganic nasal, not a free-standing /n/: it takes the place of articulation of the consonant it stands before — संगीत [sʌŋɡit̪], कांग्रेस [käŋɡres], संविधान [sʌmbid̪än], इंडिया [iɳɖijä]. Only /m n ŋ/ are contrastive in Nepali (Khatiwada 2009: 373, 377), so these are surface realisations of the one nasal slot the anusvara writes. Restricted by grapheme to the anusvara, because a written न does not assimilate the same way."
